---
/**
 * Two simulated sessions doing the same job, with a running token counter.
 *
 * READ THIS BEFORE TRUSTING ANYTHING BELOW
 *
 * The text that scrolls is RECONSTRUCTED. What a model actually emits is not
 * reproducible on demand, so these are realistic sessions of the shape the two
 * architectures produce, not recordings. "Live replay" would borrow a trace's
 * authority it would not have: there is no trace to replay. Every token figure is
 * measured: real tools/list from a live @modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem
 * session, real `f` output from the built binary, o200k_base throughout,
 * cross-checked at 260 against the figure published in /docs/measurements/.
 *
 * WHY THERE IS NO HEADLINE RATIO
 *
 * Two earlier revisions published one — 77x, then 48x — and both were wrong in the
 * direction that flattered the claim. A session is many requests, and the definitions
 * ride on all of them, which means the honest unit is billed-rate after prompt
 * caching, not "resident vs nothing".
 *
 * What kills the single ratio is that caching turns on a published constant neither
 * architecture controls: minimum cacheable length is 1,024 tokens for Sonnet and 4,096
 * for Opus and Haiku 4.5. Measured prefixes — the tools field plus system prompt,
 * everything before message history:
 *
 *   MCP  14 filesystem tools + system   1,706 tok
 *   f    one shell tool + system            57 tok
 *
 *   Sonnet  min 1,024: MCP caches  -> 2,474 tok-equivalents | f cannot  -> 171
 *   Opus    min 4,096: MCP cannot  -> 5,118                 | f cannot  -> 171
 *
 * 48x, 14x, 30x — each true under some model and false under another. Averaging them
 * would produce a number that is precise about nothing, so the table shows them
 * instead.
 *
 * The 1,024 threshold also means f cannot cache at all, at any model. Its advantage is
 * not a better cache strategy; it is carrying 1,649 fewer prefix tokens and 2,776 fewer
 * per turn, cached or not.
 *
 * Billing arithmetic, from published rates: a cache write costs 1.25x base, a read
 * 0.1x, and the 5-minute TTL refreshes free on each hit. Over three turns the first
 * request is a write — MORE expensive than base, not cheaper — and only turns two and
 * three are reads. Counting all three at read rate understates MCP by a quarter of the
 * prefix, in f's favour. That is the error class worth hunting precisely because it
 * helps you.
 *
 * f registers no tools of its own (the repo is CLI-only); the shell tool below is what
 * any harness already ships. Both sides pay for it, so it is included on both rather
 * than subtracted — a difference that survives subtraction is the difference.
 */

// From scripts/measure-streams.mjs.
const MCP = {
  tools: 14,
  /** Full tool object; resident in the tools field of every request. */
  defs: 2877,
  calls: [29, 26],
  results: [46, 236],
};
const F = {
  bashDef: 44,
  index: 57,
  calls: [15, 13],
  results: [42, 15],
};

const PREFIX = { mcp: 1706, f: 57 };
const MIN = { sonnet: 1024, opus: 4096 };
const WRITE = 1.25;
const READ = 0.1;
const TURNS = 3;

// Resident-prefix cost over the session in base-input-token equivalents: turn 1 pays
// the write, later turns pay the read on a hit, full price on a miss.
const billed = (prefix, caches) => (caches ? prefix * (WRITE + READ * (TURNS - 1)) : prefix * TURNS);

const rows = [
  { model: "Sonnet", min: MIN.sonnet, mcpCaches: PREFIX.mcp >= MIN.sonnet, fCaches: PREFIX.f >= MIN.sonnet },
  { model: "Opus / Haiku 4.5", min: MIN.opus, mcpCaches: PREFIX.mcp >= MIN.opus, fCaches: PREFIX.f >= MIN.opus },
];

// Cumulative tool payload per turn — what the counters run to.
const mcpTurns = [
  MCP.defs,
  MCP.defs * 2 + MCP.calls[0] + MCP.results[0],
  MCP.defs * 3 + MCP.calls[0] + MCP.results[0] + MCP.calls[1] + MCP.results[1],
];
const fTurns = [
  F.bashDef + F.index,
  F.bashDef + F.index + F.calls[0] + F.results[0],
  F.bashDef + F.index + F.calls[0] + F.results[0] + F.calls[1] + F.results[1],
];
const total = (t) => t.at(-1);
---

<div class="compare">
  <p class="compare-job">
    Three turns of one job, both ways. The counters are cumulative tool payload,
    measured. The text is a realistic reconstruction, not a recording.
  </p>

  <div class="compare-panes">
    <section class="compare-col" aria-label="Simulated session using MCP tools">
      <p class="compare-head">
        <span class="compare-svc">MCP</span>
        <span class="compare-sub">{MCP.tools} tools declared</span>
        <span class="compare-count" data-count-for="mcp" data-count-to={total(mcpTurns)}><b>{total(mcpTurns).toLocaleString()}</b> tokens</span>
      </p>
      <div class="stream" data-stream="mcp">
        <div class="turn">
          <p class="turn-h">turn 1 <span>{" "}{mcpTurns[0]}</span></p>
          <pre class="ln body">tools: read_text_file, write_file, edit_file,
       create_directory, list_directory, directory_tree,
       move_file, search_files, get_file_info, …
       <em>14 definitions in the request's tools field</em></pre>
        </div>
        <div class="turn">
          <p class="turn-h">turn 2 <span>{" "}{mcpTurns[1].toLocaleString()}</span></p>
          <pre class="ln asst">{`{ "type": "tool_use", "name": "read_text_file",
  "input": { "path": "/tmp/mcpsim/notes/creds.md" } }`}</pre>
          <pre class="ln tool">{`{ "content": [ { "type": "text",
  "text": "prod.db\\n  host: db.internal\\n  user: svc\\n" } ] }`}</pre>
        </div>
        <div class="turn">
          <p class="turn-h">turn 3 <span>{" "}{mcpTurns[2].toLocaleString()}</span></p>
          <pre class="ln asst">{`{ "type": "tool_use", "name": "directory_tree",
  "input": { "path": "/tmp/mcpsim", "excludePatterns": [] } }`}</pre>
          <pre class="ln tool">{`{ "content": [ { "type": "text", "text": "[
 { "name": "notes", "type": "directory",
   "children": [ { "name": "creds.md",
     "type": "file" } ] } ]" } ] }`}</pre>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="compare-col" aria-label="Simulated session using f">
      <p class="compare-head">
        <span class="compare-svc f">f</span>
        <span class="compare-sub">1 tool declared</span>
        <span class="compare-count" data-count-for="f" data-count-to={total(fTurns)}><b>{total(fTurns)}</b> tokens</span>
      </p>
      <div class="stream" data-stream="f">
        <div class="turn">
          <p class="turn-h">turn 1 <span>{" "}{fTurns[0]}</span></p>
          <pre class="ln body">tools: bash
$ f
f v0.3.3
config creds df fj gh ha providers search uck</pre>
        </div>
        <div class="turn">
          <p class="turn-h">turn 2 <span>{" "}{fTurns[1]}</span></p>
          <pre class="ln asst">{`{ "tool": "bash",
  "input": { "command": "f creds get prod.db" } }`}</pre>
          <pre class="ln tool">prod.db = sk-live-9f2c… (expires in 2h 14m)</pre>
        </div>
        <div class="turn">
          <p class="turn-h">turn 3 <span>{" "}{fTurns[2]}</span></p>
          <pre class="ln asst">{`{ "tool": "bash",
  "input": { "command": "f creds status" } }`}</pre>
          <pre class="ln tool">unlocked (167m 31s left)</pre>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <table class="cache-table">
    <caption>
      Cost of the resident prefix over {TURNS} turns, in base-input-token equivalents.
      Turn 1 is a cache <em>write</em> at {WRITE}× base; later turns read at {READ}×.
      A prefix shorter than the model's minimum cannot be cached at all.
    </caption>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th scope="col">Model</th>
        <th scope="col">Min. cacheable</th>
        <th scope="col">MCP {" "}{PREFIX.mcp.toLocaleString()} tok</th>
        <th scope="col">f {" "}{PREFIX.f} tok</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {rows.map((r) => (
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">{r.model}</th>
          <td>{r.min.toLocaleString()}</td>
          <td class={r.mcpCaches ? "cache-hit" : "cache-miss"}>
            {r.mcpCaches ? "caches" : "cannot"} · {Math.round(billed(PREFIX.mcp, r.mcpCaches)).toLocaleString()}
          </td>
          <td class={r.fCaches ? "cache-hit" : "cache-miss"}>
            {r.fCaches ? "caches" : "cannot"} · {Math.round(billed(PREFIX.f, r.fCaches)).toLocaleString()}
          </td>
        </tr>
      ))}
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <p class="compare-verdict">
    f cannot cache at any model: its whole prefix is {PREFIX.f} tokens, under every
    published minimum. MCP caches on Sonnet and cannot on Opus, where its {" "}
    {PREFIX.mcp.toLocaleString()} tokens fall under the {MIN.opus.toLocaleString()}{" "}
    minimum. So the difference is not cache strategy: f carries{" "}
    <b>{(PREFIX.mcp - PREFIX.f).toLocaleString()} fewer prefix tokens</b> and{" "}
    <b>{(MCP.defs - F.bashDef - F.index).toLocaleString()} fewer per turn</b>, on every
    model, cached or not.{" "}
    <a href="/docs/measurements/">how these were measured</a>
  </p>
</div>
